# Copy to .env.local. Both settings are optional — the defaults work for local
# development with the backend on :8000.

# Port this UI listens on. Next reads PORT natively.
PORT=8100

# --- how the browser reaches the API -------------------------------------
#
# By default it does NOT reach it directly. The browser makes same-origin
# requests to this server, and next.config.ts proxies /api/v1/* and /health*
# to the address below. No cross-origin request, so no CORS involved, and the
# UI port can change without touching the backend.
#
# Server-side only: the browser never sees this value.
API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# --- opting out of the proxy ---------------------------------------------
#
# Set this to call the API directly from the browser instead. That IS a
# cross-origin request, so the backend must list this app's exact origin in
# its CORS_ORIGINS (e.g. http://localhost:8100) or every request fails a
# preflight check. Leave it unset unless you need it.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
